# Jaguar 340 four-door saloon, 1967-1969.
#
# The final 3.4-litre Mark 2 derivative, sold alongside the 240 with the same
# slim bumpers, revised grille and Ambla interior. The Mark 2 shell with the
# 1967 detailing.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_Mark_2
#
# Dimensions 4.57 x 1.70 x 1.47 m, wheelbase 2.72 m.
#
# Shape reference: no true side elevation exists. The best is a rear
# three-quarter profile about 40 degrees off; the flank is reconciled against
# the front and rear three-quarters within the published dimensions. Three
# files titled as 340s were rejected on date or trim grounds and are recorded
# in the pack notes.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no UK brochure was consulted. British Racing Green,
# Black, Old English White and Carmen Red are period Jaguar finishes. Weights 4,
# 3, 2, 1, total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 185 km/h. Comfort 75/443, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 75. Classes 2,3.
# Dates 1967-1969 production, road tail staggered 1982-1984.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaguar-340.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/jaguar-340.dae. References: citycars/references/jaguar-340/
# (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the shell was corrected in a derivative copy because the
# existing Mark 2 master's squared nose and angular roof/rear glazing did not
# match the photographs. The existing Mark 2 asset is left untouched. No true
# side elevation or rear view exists; the best is a rear three-quarter about
# 40 degrees off, reconciled against the front view and the published dimensions.


obj=citycar
